<title>NETHERLANDS: DIARY - Dutch AEX and AMX ex-dividend dates.</title>
<headline>DIARY - Dutch AEX and AMX ex-dividend dates.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is a list of dates when component shares of the Dutch AEX and AMX stock market indices start trading ex-dividend. April 18, 1997</p>
<p>- Hagemeyer</p>
<p>- Wolters Kluwer April 21, 1997</p>
<p>- Elsevier April 23, 1997</p>
<p>- VNU</p>
<p>- Pakhoed April 25, 1997</p>
<p>- Heineken April 29, 1997</p>
<p>- Akzo Nobel May 1, 1997</p>
<p>- Wegener</p>
<p>- Internatio Mueller May 2, 1997</p>
<p>- Grolsch May 6, 1997</p>
<p>- Gist Brocades May 7, 1997</p>
<p>- KPN</p>
<p>- Unilever</p>
<p>- Ahold</p>
<p>- ING</p>
<p>- KBB (Bijenkorf) May 9, 1997</p>
<p>- Volker Stevin</p>
<p>- Boskalis</p>
<p>- ABN AMRO May 14, 1997</p>
<p>- Ahrend May 15, 1997</p>
<p>- Stad Rotterdam</p>
<p>- Vendex</p>
<p>- Royal Dutch May 16, 1997</p>
<p>- Nutricia</p>
<p>- Aegon May 19, 1997</p>
<p>Randstad May 20, 1997</p>
<p>- HBG May 22, 1997</p>
<p>- NBM-Amstelland</p>
<p>- Cap Gemini</p>
<p>- Nedlloyd May 29, 1997</p>
<p>- Fortis Amev</p>
<p>- De Boer June 2, 1997</p>
<p>- IHC Caland</p>
